# Billing — Cron triggers (manual publishers)
# UC-113: the local / manual path of the Billing crons. Cloud Scheduler publishes the same trigger in
# staging and production; these routes only publish it, behind InternalApiGuard. The job runs in the
# trigger handler, so read its structured log line (billing_issue_charges_run) to see the result.
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl     = {{backendUrl}}
@internalKey = {{$dotenv INTERNAL_API_KEY}}

### Issue the next charges (UC-113): every subscription due within 10 days, then the creation retry
POST {{baseUrl}}/cron/billing-issue-charges
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

### Sweep the subscription statuses (UC-115): overdue charges, trial end, grace end and scheduled cancels
POST {{baseUrl}}/cron/billing-status-sweep
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

### Reconcile the charges with the provider (UC-116): the at-risk scope, plus the full pass once a day
POST {{baseUrl}}/cron/billing-reconcile
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

### Self-heal (UC-140): provisioning repair, stale registration release, provider health, suspension freeze
# Read the billing_self_heal_run log line for the four step results.
POST {{baseUrl}}/cron/billing-self-heal
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

### Dunning reminders (UC-139): trial, due-soon, overdue and recovery-charge reminders for today's milestones
# Read the billing_reminders_run log line; each reminder is one shared.outbox row (a rerun writes none).
POST {{baseUrl}}/cron/billing-reminders
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

### Provider events purge (UC-114): deletes webhook inbox rows older than 30 days
# Read the billing_provider_events_purge_run log line (rows deleted, batches, limitHit).
POST {{baseUrl}}/cron/billing-provider-events-purge
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

### Without the internal key: refused with 401 (the route is internal-only, behind InternalApiGuard)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cron/billing-issue-charges
